                <pb facs="0480" n="1214" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1214"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister for foreign affairs says Dupuy’s note concerning your No. 408 received
                    to-day was prior special examination. Minister said he was disposed to grant at
                    once to consuls of the United States in Cuba all rights guaranteed to German
                    consul under the treaty of 1870.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taylor.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
